            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0612" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v04/pg580"/>

                <head>289. Memorandum From the Secretary of the Council on Foreign Economic Policy
                    (Cullen) to the Council<anchor n="0" xml:id="d289-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-12-15">December 15, 1958</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>CFEP 577—U.S. Restrictions on Imports of Oil Which Affect Canada</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Attached is a draft statement of policy on the above subject, prepared by
                        the NSC Planning Board. The draft statement has been referred by the NSC
                        Planning Board to the Council on Foreign Economic Policy for comment prior
                        to its consideration by the NSC on December 23.<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d289-f2"/></item>
                    <pb facs="0613" n="581" xml:id="pg581"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Planning Board has recommended that, if the NSC approves the draft
                        statement of policy, it be submitted to the President with a recommendation
                        that the President approve it as guidance from the standpoint of national
                        security and direct that it be taken into account by the President’s Special
                        Committee to Investigate Crude Oil Imports.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The foreign economic policy aspects of the draft statement will be
                        considered by the CFEP on December 18, 1958.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d289-f3"
                        /></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Paul H. Cullen</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lt. Col, USA</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d289-a1.xml" xpointer="d289-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
